    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given an array of intervals, return the **minimum number of intervals to remove** so that the rest don't overlap. Intervals that only touch, like `[1,2]` and `[2,3]`, don't overlap."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/5ce9a7c5-c14b-46a2-886a-6af8360c7434.svg",
      "alt": "Four intervals: 1 to 2, 2 to 3, 3 to 4 and 1 to 3. Sorted by end time, the greedy keeps 1 to 2, then 2 to 3, rejects 1 to 3 because it starts before 3, and keeps 3 to 4. One interval is removed.",
      "width": 758,
      "height": 402,
