    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "[[1,2], [2,3], [3,4], [1,3]]  ->  1   (remove [1,3])\n[[1,2], [1,2], [1,2]]         ->  2\n[[1,2], [2,3]]                ->  0"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "The idea: keep the interval that ends first"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Removing as few as possible is the same as **keeping as many as possible**. Among all intervals, the one that **ends earliest** is always a safe first choice: whatever the best answer keeps first, swapping it for the earliest-ending interval can't cause a new overlap, because that one ends even sooner. After choosing it, discard everything that overlaps it and repeat with what's left."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sorting by end time turns that into one pass: walk the intervals in order of end, keep an interval if it starts at or after the end of the last one kept, and skip it otherwise. This is the classic **interval scheduling** greedy."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. Dynamic programming over intervals sorted by start"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A safe but slower route: sort by start, and let `keep[i]` be the most intervals that can be kept ending with interval `i` — one plus the best `keep[j]` over earlier intervals `j` that end by the time `i` starts."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function eraseOverlapIntervals(intervals) {\n  const a = [...intervals].sort((x, y) => x[0] - y[0]);   // by start time\n  const keep = new Array(a.length).fill(1);\n  let most = 0;\n  for (let i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {\n      if (a[j][1] <= a[i][0]) keep[i] = Math.max(keep[i], keep[j] + 1);   // i can follow j\n    }\n    most = Math.max(most, keep[i]);\n  }\n  return a.length - most;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def erase_overlap_intervals(intervals):\n    a = sorted(intervals)                 # by start time\n    keep = [1] * len(a)\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        for j in range(i):\n            if a[j][1] <= a[i][0]:        # i can follow j\n                keep[i] = max(keep[i], keep[j] + 1)\n    return len(a) - max(keep, default=0)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int eraseOverlapIntervals(int[][] intervals) {\n    int[][] a = intervals.clone();\n    Arrays.sort(a, (x, y) -> Integer.compare(x[0], y[0]));   // by start time\n    int[] keep = new int[a.length];\n    int most = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < a.length; i++) {\n        keep[i] = 1;\n        for (int j = 0; j < i; j++) {\n            if (a[j][1] <= a[i][0]) keep[i] = Math.max(keep[i], keep[j] + 1);   // i can follow j\n        }\n        most = Math.max(most, keep[i]);\n    }\n    return a.length - most;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int eraseOverlapIntervals(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    vector<vector<int>> a = intervals;\n    sort(a.begin(), a.end());                                 // by start time\n    vector<int> keep(a.size(), 1);\n    int most = 0;\n    for (size_t i = 0; i < a.size(); i++) {\n        for (size_t j = 0; j < i; j++) {\n            if (a[j][1] <= a[i][0]) keep[i] = max(keep[i], keep[j] + 1);   // i can follow j\n        }\n        most = max(most, keep[i]);\n    }\n    return a.size() - most;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n²), space O(n).** Correct, but it considers every pair."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Greedy: sort by end, keep what fits"
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "non-overlapping-intervals",
      "caption": "Sorted by end time, keep an interval whenever it starts after the last kept one ends."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function eraseOverlapIntervals(intervals) {\n  const sorted = [...intervals].sort((a, b) => a[1] - b[1]);   // by end time\n  let kept = 0, lastEnd = -Infinity;\n  for (const [start, end] of sorted) {\n    if (start >= lastEnd) {          // fits after the last kept interval: keep it\n      kept++;\n      lastEnd = end;\n    }                                // otherwise it overlaps: remove it\n  }\n  return sorted.length - kept;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def erase_overlap_intervals(intervals):\n    kept, last_end = 0, float(\"-inf\")\n    for start, end in sorted(intervals, key=lambda iv: iv[1]):   # by end time\n        if start >= last_end:             # fits after the last kept interval: keep it\n            kept += 1\n            last_end = end\n    return len(intervals) - kept"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "int eraseOverlapIntervals(int[][] intervals) {\n    int[][] sorted = intervals.clone();\n    Arrays.sort(sorted, (a, b) -> Integer.compare(a[1], b[1]));   // by end time\n    int kept = 0;\n    long lastEnd = Long.MIN_VALUE;\n    for (int[] iv : sorted) {\n        if (iv[0] >= lastEnd) {          // fits after the last kept interval: keep it\n            kept++;\n            lastEnd = iv[1];\n        }                                // otherwise it overlaps: remove it\n    }\n    return sorted.length - kept;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "int eraseOverlapIntervals(vector<vector<int>>& intervals) {\n    vector<vector<int>> sorted = intervals;\n    sort(sorted.begin(), sorted.end(), [](auto& a, auto& b) { return a[1] < b[1]; });   // by end time\n    int kept = 0;\n    long long lastEnd = LLONG_MIN;\n    for (auto& iv : sorted) {\n        if (iv[0] >= lastEnd) {          // fits after the last kept interval: keep it\n            kept++;\n            lastEnd = iv[1];\n        }                                // otherwise it overlaps: remove it\n    }\n    return sorted.size() - kept;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n log n), space O(n)** for the copy. One pass after the sort."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
