    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Sorting by **start** and keeping greedily doesn't work: `[1,100]` starts first but blocks everything. Sorting by **end** is the whole trick."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Touching intervals** — `[1,2]` and `[2,3]` both stay: compare with `>=`.",
        "**Identical intervals** — keep one, remove the rest.",
        "**One long interval covering many short ones** — remove the long one, not the short ones.",
        "**Negative times** — start `lastEnd` below any possible start."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Minimum Number of Arrows to Burst Balloons** — the same greedy: one arrow per kept interval, with touching counting as overlap.",
        "**Maximum Length of Pair Chain** — keep the longest chain: exactly the number of intervals kept here.",
        "**Meeting Rooms II** — instead of removing meetings, give overlapping ones more rooms. Next lesson."
      ]
    }
  ],
